Z||000015||1FST2M6||11-16-2001||04:39 PM||||Konig are awsome! jump all over em! they suck to clean but look INSANE! you need em.. 17 up front 18 out back!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||DKOV||11-16-2001||06:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fast_5_rim.jpg">  <BR>These are my rims.  Fast 5 with 215/45/17 front and 225/45/17 rear with Kumho Ecxsta rubber.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The only problem with getting those great big rims is how TINY the stock brakes look back there!  It bugged me when I put 17s on my 88 GT too...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>So, I put 13 inch brakes on my GT!  Talk about a FULL wheel!  The brakes won't even fit in anything smaller than a 17 inch rim!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000017||FieroRacer||11-16-2001||11:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DKOV:<BR><B> So, I put 13 inch brakes on my GT!  Talk about a FULL wheel!  The brakes won't even fit in anything smaller than a 17 inch rim!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you use Held Motorsports 13" Kit?  I'm thinking about that for my GT.  How is it?||||reg||1
Z||000018||Jay||11-16-2001||11:36 PM||||It's true!  It's not so bad on the rear because I've got the Cadillac rotors, but the fronts (like in the photo) seem so small.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Formula88||11-17-2001||12:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>Konig are awsome! jump all over em! they suck to clean but look INSANE! you need em.. 17 up front 18 out back!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, if you <B>insist!</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>How's this sound, then:<BR>Front: 17x7 with 225/45-17<BR>Rear: 18x8.5 with 255/35-18<P>That cuts down on my tire choices, though.  I was hoping to go with Bridgestone Potenza RE730's, cuz they're a good balance of price vs. performance.  But in the 18's, I might as well go with Pole Position S-03's or PZero's.  ||||reg||1
Z||000020||DKOV||11-17-2001||02:10 AM||||FieroRacer:<P>Yessir!  Held's they are.  Quite possibly the most incredible looking thing I've done to the car.  At least the most noticable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>They have a really cool gold colored, zing plated finish with the silver pad wear area.  A VERY cool look.  The Calipers are Wilwood and are a four piston billet.  Also very cool.  This is the only brake upgrade kit that includes the e-brake assemblies that do not have to be "specially designed" to work with the stock system.<P>The kit also includes a MASSIVE brake master cylinder and bias proportioning valve.  As well as the steel braded lines and all needed hardware.<P>VERY comprehensive and VERY cool!  I highly recommend it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just make sure and tell them that Scott from Vancouver, WA sent ya!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000021||Nashco||11-17-2001||03:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DKOV:<BR><B>FieroRacer:<P>Yessir!  Held's they are.  Quite possibly the most incredible looking thing I've done to the car.  At least the most noticable   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>They have a really cool gold colored, zing plated finish with the silver pad wear area.  A VERY cool look.  The Calipers are Wilwood and are a four piston billet.  Also very cool.  This is the only brake upgrade kit that includes the e-brake assemblies that do not have to be "specially designed" to work with the stock system.<P>The kit also includes a MASSIVE brake master cylinder and bias proportioning valve.  As well as the steel braded lines and all needed hardware.<P>VERY comprehensive and VERY cool!  I highly recommend it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just make sure and tell them that Scott from Vancouver, WA sent ya!<P>DKOV -</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So, they were pretty, but did they perform like 13" brakes?  I'm looking at a brake swap (just got 17s today) and performance is the most important aspect, looks are unimportant.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000022||DKOV||11-17-2001||03:07 PM||||Do they perform?  Oh yes!<P>I have race my Fiero GT at PIR for the past two seasons.  I race in the SPO class - GT<P>The whole point of the conversions was to help in performance.  Which they do!  If you are planning on racing at all... street, solo, touring, etc.  THESE are the answer!<P>A bit more weight and rotating mass than the stock setup but WELL worth it.<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
